From 49384545092781e266dfc8c6ae574291b65cb89f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Ewen <ryan.ewen@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 13:37:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Delete the Claude transcript when a chat is disposed

Disposing a chat tore down its live SDK session and dropped its backing,
but left the transcript on disk. Nothing ever removed it, so a session
the user deleted reappeared the next time the list was built.

Delete the SDK session as part of dispose, which is what the Copilot
agent already does. `truncateChat` makes this exact call, so the
capability is not new.

This is safe because every `disposeChat` caller means to destroy the
chat: rollback of a half-created chat or session, session teardown, and
an explicit chat delete. Teardown that must resume later goes through
`releaseChat`, which is untouched.

A transcript that cannot be removed is logged and swallowed rather than
failing the dispose: the chat is already out of the catalog by that
point, so rejecting would strand the caller with a chat it cannot
address.
